//CTP Editor Structure file
//For more detailed comments see advance.ces

0.3 //Version number

#%047%047	//Comment charachter in data file
%032%009	//Delimiter charachters in data file
		// (use %nnn for ASCII ref)
:		//Break on right quasi-delimiter
}{		//Break on left quasi-delimiter

1 // Format

f //Whether this has a number at the top (num of entries)
t //Whether this has a tree structure
t //Whether this file references GL entries (see below)
t //Whether this file has entries in gl_str.txt
f //Whether the entries have an article
f //Whether this file is the GL icon file
f //Whether this structure file describes formatting of fields
  // (i.e. whether it has the LBF and LAF columns below)

//Name			Comp	PByDef	AMult	NumArgs
	//Type		DefaultValue	Comment
DefaultIcon		t	t	f	1
	uniticon.ces	ICON_%n		Icon ID to be used for this building. Must be a valid Icon ID from UnitIcon.txt 
Description		t	t	f	1
	0		DESCRIPTION_IMPROVE_ACADEMY	This string is not used within the game but must reference a valid String ID from one of the string files.  
EnableAdvance		f	t	f	1
	advance.ces	ADVANCE_	Advance ID that enables construction of this building. Must be a valid Advance ID from Advance.txt 
ObsoleteAdvance		f	f	f	1
	advance.ces	ADVANCE_	Advance ID that renders this building obsolete. Up to 5 ObsoleteAdvances can be defined. Must be a valid Advance ID from Advance.txt 
PrerequisiteBuilding	f	f	t	1
	buildings.ces	IMPROVE_	Building ID of building that must be built before this building can be contructed. Any number of PrerequisiteBuildings can be defined. 
ProductionCost		t	t	f	1
	0		1000		Production cost to build this building 
Upkeep			t	t	f	1
	0		10		Commerce cost to maintain this building 

DefendersPercent	f	f	f	1
	0		15		Amount to add to Defense rating of unit's garrisoned in city with this building. NOTE: This is not a percent but a flat amount added. 
HappyInc		f	f	f	1
	0		1		Amount to raise Happiness in cities with this building 
ProductionPercent	f	f	f	1
	0		0.15		Fraction to increase Production output 
FoodPercent		f	f	f	1
	0		0.15		Fraction to increase Food output 
CommercePercent		f	f	f	1
	0		0.15		Fraction to increase Gold output. NOTE: This actually effects only Gold output not Commerce. 
SciencePercent		f	f	f	1
	0		0.15		Fraction to increase Science output 
FoodVat			f	f	f	1
	0		1		Set the building as food vat. The value defines the amount of pollution produced per unit of food created. 
LowerCrime		f	f	f	1
	0		-0.1		Fraction to modify Crime. NOTE: This value is an INCREASE. 
PreventConversion	f	f	f	1
	0		0.4		Chance of stopping a foreign religious unit from converting this city. Valid values: 0.0 - 1.0 
PreventSlavery		f	f	f	1
	0		0.4		Chance of stopping foreign slavers from Slave Raiding this city. Valid values: 0.0 - 1.0 
LowerPeaceMovement	f	f	f	1
	0		-0.2		Modifier to the War Discontent amount. NOTE: This value is an INCREASE. 
GoldPerCitizen		f	f	f	1
	0		1		Amount of Gold per citizen this building generates. 
ProtectFromBioAgents	f	f	f	1
	0		0.5		Chance of stopping Infector attacks on this city. Valid values: 0.0 - 1.0 
ProtectFromNanoVirus	f	f	f	1
	0		0.5		Chance of stopping Eco-Terrorist attacks on this city. Valid values: 0.0 - 1.0 
SciencePerPop		f	f	f	1
	0		1		Amount of Science per citizen this building generates 
RaiseOvercrowdingLevel	f	f	f	1
	0		1		Amount to increase the level where overcrowding begins. 
RaiseMaxPopulation	f	f	f	1
	0		1		Amount to increase the maximum population 
StarvationProtection	f	f	f	1
	0		5		Number of turns this building can prevent starvation. 
OffenseBonusLand	f	f	f	1
	0		20		Amount to add to Attack rating of unit's garrisoned within this city when attacking land units 
OffenseBonusWater	f	f	f	1
	0		20		Amount to add to Attack rating of unit's garrisoned within this city when attacking naval units 
OffenseBonusAir		f	f	f	1
	0		20		Amount to add to Attack rating of unit's garrisoned within this city when attacking aerial units 
PopulationPollutionPercent	f	f	f	1
	0		0.5		Fraction to modify pollution created by population.
ProductionPollutionPercent	f	f	f	1
	0		0.5		Fraction to modify pollution created by production. 
PollutionAmount		f	f	f	1
	0		0		Flat amount of pollution created by this building 
Capitol			f	f	f	0	This building set the Capitol city. Only one building can have this flag and it can only exist in one city in the empire. Building a new one will cause the old one to be removed. 
DoubleTelevangelists	f	f	f	0	This building causes Televangelists to have twice the change of succeeding against the host city. 
Airport			f	f	f	0	This building is an airport. 
NoUnhappyPeople		f	f	f	0	This building prevent people from becoming unhappy 
NoRushBuyPenalty	f	f	f	0	This building removes the RushBuy penalty 
AllowGrunts		f	f	f	0	This flag is not used by the game. 
ProtectFromNukes	f	f	f	0	This building protects the city from nuclear strikes. 
Television		f	f	f	0	This building is a Television. 
CityWalls		f	f	f	0	This building is a City Wall 
IsReligious		f	f	f	0	This building is a religious building 
ForceField		f	f	f	0	This building is a Force Field 
CantBuildInSea		f	f	f	0	This building cannot be built in Ocean Cities 
CantBuildOnLand		f	f	f	0	This building cannot be built in Land Cities 
Cathedral		f	f	f	0	This building is a Cathedral 
Brokerage		f	f	f	0	This building is a Brokerage 
NuclearPlant		f	f	f	0	This building is a Nuclear Plant 
CoastalBuilding		f	f	f	0	This building can only be built in coastal cities 
GLHidden		f	f	f	0	This flag causes this building to not be displayed in the Great Library 
@ //End of fields

PrerequisiteBuilding

//Stuff on the right
(I)	buildings.ces	PrerequisiteBuilding
@

DefaultIcon //GL icon field
DATABASE_BUILDINGS //Name of database for GL hyperlinks
IMPROVE_  //The prefix which identifies this file in gl_str.txt
